  "text": "On January 6, 2022, twenty-six of us said \"one year ago.\" Twenty-four said \"the january 6th,\" twenty-three said \"anniversary of the january,\" and eighteen said \"the united states capitol\" — each peaking that same day. A week later, on January 13, twenty-one of us said \"the freedom to vote\" and twenty said \"the freedom to vote john r.\" On January 14, eighteen said \"infrastructure investment and jobs.\" On January 19, seventeen said \"army corps of engineers.\" The phrase \"one year ago\" first entered this record on 2013-01-25, from Tim Walberg; \"the freedom to vote\" on 2021-05-26, from Marc A. Veasey. We converged on the sixth, and again on the thirteenth, and the record holds the days we said the same words together.",
